UID:10010771-1783107000-1783117800@visityolo.com
SUMMARY:Davis Musical Theatre Presents: RENT
DESCRIPTION:Davis Musical Theatre Presents: RENT – June 26 through July 19\, 2026\nUnderwritten by Nancy Dunne\nSet in the East Village of New York City\, Rent is about falling in love\, finding your voice and living for today. Winner of the Tony Award for Best Musical and the Pulitzer Prize for Drama\, Rent has become a pop cultural phenomenon. with songs that rock and a story that resonates with audiences of all ages. Based loosely on Puccini’s La Boheme\, Jonathan Larson’s Rent follows a year in the life of a group of impoverished young artists and musicians struggling to survive and create in New York’s Lower East Side\, under the shadow of HIV/AIDS. How these young bohemians negotiate their dreams\, loves and conflicts provides the narrative thread to this groundbreaking musical. \nRecommended for theater goers 13 & up \nDirected by Kyle Jackson\nChoreographed by Kyle Jackson
URL:https://visityolo.com/event/rent/2026-07-03/
LOCATION:Davis Musical Theatre Company (DMTC)\, The Jean Henderson Performing Arts Center\, 607 Pena Drive\, Davis
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visityolo.com/wp-content/uploads/RENT.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Davis Musical Theatre Company (DMTC)":MAILTO:info@dmtc.org
END:VEVENT
